  "overview": {
    "title": "The legendary sculpture of Ifrane",
    "p1": "The Stone Lion (Gouraud Lion) is Ifrane's most famous landmark, carved directly out of a limestone outcrop in a tranquil public park near the town centre. Sculpted during the 1930s, it serves as a poignant tribute to the last wild Atlas lions that once roamed these mountain forests.",
    "p2": "Visitors do not need tickets or guides to view the statue. It sits in an accessible green space where travellers frequently stop to take memorable photographs and enjoy a relaxing stroll amidst the alpine atmosphere of the town.",
    "p3": "Whether you visit early in the morning when the park is quiet or during the afternoon glow, this iconic monument is an unmissable stop for anyone exploring Ifrane."
